[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Add the following line to /boot/loader.conf on boards with a YT921x switch:

yt921x_load="YES"

To persist four access VLANs per switch, add this to /etc/rc.conf:

yt921x_config_enable="YES"
yt921x_config_switches="etherswitch0:101,102,103,104 etherswitch1:201,202,203,204"

The four VLAN IDs map to external ports 0 through 3. Repeat a VLAN ID to
place multiple ports in one hardware-switched group, for example:

yt921x_config_switches="etherswitch0:101,101,103,103"

List each unique VLAN only once in vlans_eqosN so each group has one vlan(4)
interface (for the example above: vlans_eqos0="vlan101 vlan103").

Validate without changing hardware, then apply the policy:

service yt921x_config validate
service yt921x_config start

Configure the corresponding FreeBSD vlan(4) interfaces through the standard
rc.conf vlans_eqos0/vlans_eqos1 and ifconfig variables.  The service configures
only switch VLAN/PVID membership and deliberately does not assign IP addresses.
Set ifconfig_eqos0="up" and ifconfig_eqos1="up" when using both CPU links.

EOM
}
]
